	 ('440d3ea2-7f73-4638-acc0-b27d464cd821'::uuid,'title:Making Spring Boot, OpenAPI, and @Transactional play nice with Arrow''s Either, description:Arrow’s Either is a very useful tool to propagate business errors, but integrating it with Spring Boot is not straightforward. Spring assumes exceptions for error flow like @Transactional rollback, and OpenAPI-generator expects ExceptionHandler for non-200 responses.

In this talk, we’ll show how we wired Either into a Spring Boot + OpenAPI stack, overcoming ACID pitfalls despite freely mixing @Transactional, TransactionOperations, and Either.

