	 ('19e8cb61-a5a1-4645-a93e-d30e31ef9cb5'::uuid,'title:Exploring and Analyzing Data as a Kotlin Developer, description:What can data science bring to Kotlin developers? How can we make it as easy as possible for Kotlin developers to start handling data using the tools they already know and love?

In this talk, we''ll find out how easy it is to get started, explore and modify data received from an API without installing complex frameworks, learning an entirely new language, or even leaving your IDE!

We''ll dive into the work of the Kotlin Data Science team at JetBrains. This includes tools like Kotlin Notebook in IntelliJ, the open-source Kotlin DataFrame library (which I''m personally involved in) and its first-of-a-kind compiler plugin, and Kandy, an open-source Kotlin-like plotting DSL.

We''ll use Kotlin notebooks as a powerful, flexible, yet familiar programming tool; parse, wrangle, and explore typed data from a simple API using DataFrame, and plot the results with Kandy.

Finally, we''ll have a small look at what the experimental DataFrame compiler plugin can do and how it might change the way you program Kotlin code in the future!','{"id": "6602aa2618a2438290747e6a6b9d4e4b", "room": "Upperdeck", "title": "Exploring and Analyzing Data as a Kotlin Developer", "endsAt": 1764248400000, "category": "[Fast Forward]", "dayIndex": 1, "speakers": "[Jolan Rensen]", "startsAt": 1764246600000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2025-11-27", "durationMinutes": 30, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2025-11-27T14:00:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2025-11-27T13:30:00"}','[-0.013640862,0.005854154,0.0040226867,-0.07478094,0.032324206,0.013652755,-0.060937908,0.02785257,-0.014449562,-0.010376331,0.03058788,-0.014556596,0.019908285,-0.019373117,0.027448222,0.013319761,-0.027162798,0.00861622,0.042218886,0.07497123,0.0052149245,-0.02770986,0.049330685,0.016185887,0.046405096,-0.031158727,-0.059653502,-0.0012539306,0.022108424,-0.029565113,-0.0023309581,-0.022417633,-1.0243469e-05,-0.03422703,0.049283113,-0.004822467,0.023583112,-0.011458562,-0.0072188345,-0.009508168,-0.035368722,-0.05632356,-0.009900626,0.03805646,-0.0059017246,0.01565072,-0.037675895,-0.00863406,-0.02119269,0.005301146,-0.07616049,-0.01601939,0.031753357,0.048236564,-0.026306529,0.00055598107,-0.0055538644,0.027495792,0.002476643,-0.023737717,0.044573627,-0.011077997,0.01286784,0.031253867,-0.058559377,0.0024558308,-0.025212405,-0.0060474095,-0.013462473,0.016863769,0.04531097,0.002327985,-0.06341158,0.030159744,-0.0149014825,-0.036914766,-0.035344936,0.009817378,0.019313654,-0.019361224,-0.007866983,0.026211387,-0.00931194,-0.00031757075,-0.02195382,-0.017054051,-0.045239616,-0.04840306,-0.04588182,0.017101621,-0.011595327,-0.00049651787,-0.027947713,0.018053032,0.10170589,0.053659607,0.018160067,0.019087693,0.026829803,-0.00018108408,0.0294224,-0.008039427,0.004412171,-0.027733644,0.06983361,0.03710505,0.05860695,-0.05294605,-0.021466222,-0.018100604,-0.093095616,-0.0326572,0.01307